  "$comment": "TASK-1005 §13 — the catalogue-first residency view, PINNED by the orchestrator before the redesign lanes branched (L-RCAT produces it, L-RUI consumes it). GET /api/v1/admin/model-residency/catalogue; same auth as the rest of admin/model-residency (platform admin, tenant-less; the BFF never forwards a working tenant to this prefix). `services[]` lists EVERY self-hosted AiModel (deploymentKind SELF_HOSTED, not DELETED) grouped by the workload that runs it (`AiModel.servedBy` normalised: stt, stt-worker, nlp, lm-studio), loaded or not; cloud rows are excluded because nothing can load them. Service order is fixed: stt, stt-worker, lm-studio, nlp. `status` is plain: loaded | loading | unloading | not_loaded. `usage.uses[]` is the reverse index model → consumers across ALL tenants: role `primary` (Agent.modelId), `fallback` (AgentModelFallback), `routing` (AiRoutingPolicy candidate for guardrail/NLP/judge tasks); only ACTIVE/PUBLISHED agents count. `liveConsultation` is true when any consumer is on the live path (the implicit PINNED rule). `keepPolicy.kind` maps PINNED→always, WARM→warm, ON_DEMAND→on_demand, with a human `label` and `reason`. `size` prefers the MEASURED footprint (`AiModel.observedMemoryMb`, or the resident report) and falls back to the catalogue estimate (`memorySizeMb`) with `source` saying which. `actions` lists what the UI may offer for this row right now (e.g. no `unload` while not loaded; `unload` still offered while in flight — the API answers 409 IN_FLIGHT and the UI asks for force + reason). Suggestions are the shadow-mode recommendations rewritten as one plain sentence each.",
